{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"a29d5859530e551c9c63051e6b73ecbf9e195803"},"timestamp":1576075438,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWU1MzY0MTY0MTY=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3919","origin":"github"},"title":"Datalad status null when there are changes to commit","message":"#### What is the problem?\nRunning `datalad status` after `datalad remove` shows no output, but `git status` shows changes to be commited. Not sure if this is normal.\n\n#### What steps will reproduce the problem?\nCreate a a testme subdataset. Save the superdataset. Remove the subdataset, and run `datalad status; git status`. My log:\n```sh\n[dorian@mri processed]$ datalad remove --nocheck testme\nremove(ok): /DATA/FEDERATED_DATASETS/study1/data/processed/testme (dataset)\n[dorian@mri processed]$\n[dorian@mri processed]$ git status\nOn branch master\nChanges not staged for commit:\n  (use \"git add/rm \u003cfile\u003e...\" to update what will be committed)\n  (use \"git checkout -- \u003cfile\u003e...\" to discard changes in working directory)\n\n        deleted:    testme\n\nno changes added to commit (use \"git add\" and/or \"git commit -a\")\n[dorian@mri processed]$ datalad status\n[dorian@mri processed]$\n```\n\n#### What version of DataLad are you using (run `datalad --version`)? On what operating system (consider running `datalad wtf`)?\ndatalad 0.12.0rc6 on CentOS 7\n\n#### Is there anything else that would be useful to know in this context?\nNo.\n\n#### Have you had any success using DataLad before? (to assess your expertise/prior luck.  We would welcome your testimonial additions to https://github.com/datalad/datalad/wiki/Testimonials as well)\nN/A","files":null}]}